  "notes": "Written for the Pacific francophone press (Tahiti, Nouvelle-Caledonie): includes territorial-administration wording ('délibération', 'arrêté', 'mercuriale', 'prix homologué', 'caisse de compensation', 'bouclier tarifaire') alongside metropolitan legal vocabulary. Deliberately dropped the bare nouns 'hausse', 'baisse', 'décision' and 'gel': they dominate ordinary price-reporting prose with no state actor present, and 'gel' also means frost; kept 'gel des prix' as the compound instead. Subject nouns (carburant, essence, énergie, alimentation, riz) are excluded so the two-signal design holds."
